<h1>Define 2D Section</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>2D Sections &gt; Define</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">or by pressing</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Adjust Section Plane</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US"><b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;">button</i></b></span> <span lang="EN-US">in the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Inspection</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">toolbar.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">This command creates/modifies 2D section plane in the current view.</span></p>
<p class="Warning"><span lang="EN-US">Define option is disabled and 2D sections can not be created when:</span></p>
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li class="kadov-p-CWarning">
<p class="Warning"><span lang="EN-US">the reference is a datum entity</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CWarning">
<p class="Warning"><span lang="EN-US">the entity to compare is Polylines, Point cloud or Probe Points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Action</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: Call the</span> <span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Define 2D section</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>plane</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">command and a dialog will appear.</span></p>
<p><img src="../Inspection_Mode_files/define_2d_section.gif" width="216px" height="471px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head">Fast Definition section</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OXY</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OYZ</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">and</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OZX</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">buttons</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Define a section plane parallel to one of the co-ordinate system planes.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Datum</span> button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:normal;">Define section using an already created datum plane. This option is not active if there is no available datum plane. If there are datum planes in the document, then select one and press</span> <span class="Button">Datum</span> <span style="font-weight:normal;">button to display it.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Section of View</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Interactive section plane creation using 2 points. If this option is chosen, the dialog will be closed automatically. The cursor will be transformed in <img src="../Images/image042.gif" width="22px" height="23px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt="">&#160;. When the start and the end points are captured, the dialog will appear again.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">Hold down the Ctrl button from the keyboard during section definition to create interactive section plane parallel to one of the X or Y viewport axes.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="font-weight:normal; text-decoration:underline;">Example for Section of View definition</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP164020484" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><b><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../Images/image043.gif" width="527px" height="417px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></b></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="font-style:normal; text-decoration:none;">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Detailed Definition section:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Point</span> <span lang="EN-US">button</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Enables direct capturing of a point co-ordinates. When activating this button the dialog will disappear and the cursor will be transformed in <img src="../Images/image044.gif" width="25px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt="">. After capturing a point from the compared entity the dialog will appear again.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-style:italic; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="font-style:italic; text-decoration:underline;">Example for capturing point</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP271654218" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../Images/image045.gif" width="503px" height="417px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">Fields</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">First 3 text fields contain the X, Y and Z co-ordinates of the central point of the defined plane. By default these values are 0. They will be updated by:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Manually typing new XYZ co-ordinates</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Loading co-ordinates from a datum plane (is this option is selected in Fast definition section)</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Capturing co-ordinates of a point directly from the viewport using the <img src="../Images/image046.gif" width="37px" height="18px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt="">&#160;button.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Calculating the co-ordinates when the option Section of view is used.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">The 3 text fields for Normal contain the X, Y and Z co-ordinates of the plane normal. By default these values are 0. They will be updated by:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Manually typing new XYZ values for the normal</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Loading values from a datum plane normal (is this option is selected in Fast definition section)</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Getting values from one of the co-ordinate system planes (if one of the OXY, OYZ and OZX radio buttons is used in Fast definition section).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Calculating the values for normal when the option Section of view is used.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">Offset text field</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">The offset value for the plane should be manually typed in the box. There will be no visible result until the <img src="../Inspection_Mode_files/define_2d_section_2.gif" width="84px" height="23px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt="">&#160;is not pressed. By default the offset value is 0 and the button is disabled.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for single plane definition</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP162008159" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Inspection_Mode_files/define_2d_section_3.gif" width="529px" height="421px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="font-style:normal; text-decoration:none;">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Multiple planes section</p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">This section offers possibility to create many report pages at once. It is very useful when needed to have inspection 2D sections at equal distance from each other. Check the box at the top of the section to enable the commands for multiple sectioning.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Count spin</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">control:</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Use the arrows on right or type in the box the number of pages, you want to create.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">Symmetry box</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Check the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Symmetry</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">box if you want to create same number of pages on both sides of the defined section plane. In this case you will have 2xCount No+1 pages created.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Offset</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Type in the box a value for the plane offset. By default it is 0.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"><br>
* The offset for multiple planes can not be 0. In this case a warning message will appear.<br>
* If some of the section planes pass out of the object extents, new section pages will be created only for the planes that cross the object. In this case less number of pages will be created, than defined.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP162050351" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Inspection_Mode_files/define_2d_section_4.gif" width="527px" height="419px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="parameterstitle">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span class="Button">Remove</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span><span lang="EN-US">:</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Deletes the section plane from the current page. If there is no section plane defined in the current view, the button will be grayed.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span class="Button">Preview</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span><span lang="EN-US">:</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Visualize all changes made in the above dialog sections.</span></p>
<p class="Warning"><span lang="EN-US">Important: Some changes of the dialog boxes are not automatically updated in the view (manually input of co-ordinate values for example). That is why it is recommended to use always Preview button when some changes in the dialog have been made.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Cancel button</b>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Cancel all the changes and restore the previous inspection view.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b><span class="Button">OK</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">or</span> <b><span class="Button">Create New Pages</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b><span lang="EN-US">:</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">This button has two functionalities:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>OK</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">– appears when there is a single section plane defined/modified in the current view. In this case all changes are accepted and respectively the view is updated.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Create New Pages</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">– appears when multiple section planes are defined in the current view. In this case, after closing the dialog, multiple new report pages will be added to the list. Each of them will appear in 2D view aligned to its section plane. By default each report page will have name S x.xxxx, where x.xxxx represent the offset from the initial plane.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a5" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for created multiple pages</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP501633983" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Inspection_Mode_files/define_2d_section_5.gif" width="189px" height="105px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></p>
</div>
